==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|vehement|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈviː.ə.məntli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-vehemently.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ve|he|ment|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[vehement]] manner; expressing with a [[strong]] or [[forceful]] [[attitude]].
#: {{coi|en|'''vehemently''' opposed}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1936|author=Rollo Ahmed|title=The Black Art|publisher=Long|location=London|page=50|passage=The Rabbis adjured her to endow the young man with his former virility, but she '''vehemently''' refused to do so.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1954|month=November|author=Frank Hewitt|title=The First Decade of British 4-6-0 Locomotives—1|journal=Railway Magazine|page=752|text=Critics were '''vehemently''' outspoken; but while they fretted about looks, they missed the cleverer points in the design itself.}}
#* {{quote-web|en
|date=October 29, 2011
|author=Phil McNulty
|title=Chelsea 3 - 5 Arsenal
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/15413593.stm
|page=
|passage=And it was a miserable afternoon for Chelsea and England captain {{w|John Terry}} at the end of a week in which has he faced allegations of racial abuse against QPR's {{w|Anton Ferdinand}} - claims he '''vehemently''' denies.}}

